# Everything in this directory is consumed by Linux — bash (EC2 user-data),
# Docker Compose, and Caddy. Pin LF so a Windows checkout can never commit a
# CRLF bootstrap.sh, which would fail on boot with the famously unhelpful
# "/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory".
#
# Scoped to this directory on purpose: a repo-root *.sh rule would renormalise
# every existing shell script and produce a large unrelated diff.
* text eol=lf
